all the lives lost and disrupted are  hard to take in one of the hardest hit  places in ukraine is the northern city  of cherniv amnesty international says an  airstrike in early march involved at  least eight unguided bombs that  indiscriminately hit civilians the city  played a key role in preventing russian  troops from advancing into the capital  kiev  russia has since retreated from the area  our europe bureau chief crystal  gamansing got a firsthand look at what  was left behind  some scars of war are obvious charred  buildings with gaping holes and  shattered glass  others are buried deep inside survivors  at the time of the explosion i was very  close to the place ighor markovic  recalls hearing the roar of an airplane  engine and seeing it fly low he didn't  need to explain what he saw next instead  he showed us his phone and a video  transporting us back two months to march  3rd  [Music]  the chaos the sound of people screaming  the bodies on the ground the images are  hard to watch but ihor  lived it  see the line here at the place where  they are standing now  you can see the leg was blown off  amnesty international says up to eight  unguided bombs were dropped here killing  at least 47 people human rights watch  was unable to identify any legitimate  military targets in the area and  concluded this strike could constitute a  warcraft  i don't see any logic in this wall  except to destroy and kill people  [Music]  at saint catherine's cathedral  worshipers share prayers to keep those  on the front lines safe and their  families at home supported  chernihev was besieged for weeks it  looked bleak there was no power no water  or food  700 deaths here have been directly  linked to the war  and those are just the ones that show  obvious signs of trauma  yuri pollock has worked for more than 20  years in forensics and has never  experienced anything like it  most of my friends do not believe what  happened in our country and want to wake  up on 21st of february in peace they  have never seen such things even in  nightmares  the last of the invading russian forces  retreated in april but for survivors the  pain is still palpable  crystal gomansen global news chinese  ukraine
 

